# Implementation Plan — `cpp-navigator`

**Scope:** Rust implementation of the LLM-optimized C++ codebase navigator.
**Derived from:** `docs/requirements.md` (PRD) and `docs/design-specs.md`.
**Branch:** `rust-implementation`.

This document is the phased build plan. Each phase is independently committable
and leaves the tool in a working state. Section references (§) point at
`design-specs.md` unless noted.

---

## Locked-in decisions

These were confirmed during planning and govern every phase:

| Topic | Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Language | **Rust** (single lib + two bins) | One static binary, instant startup, first-class tree-sitter + ripgrep crates (§13). |
| Architecture | **Hybrid:** tree-sitter default (Stage 1), libclang opt-in (Stage 2) | B for zero-config speed, A for true semantics; degradation ladder falls out naturally (§4). |
| Text search | **Embed ripgrep's crates** (`ignore` + `grep-*`), no external `rg` | Self-contained, zero-egress, honors `.gitignore` (§13, open-decision §15.5). |
| Stage 2 backend | Behind `--features semantic` + runtime `--semantic` | Keeps the default build free of any system library (libclang). |
| Persistent index | **None in v1** — prefilter + in-process parse cache | Point queries don't need it; deferred to future work (§10, §16). |
| Exit codes | `0` = well-formed answer incl. `not_found`; `2` = usage; `3` = internal | Simple agent control flow — always read stdout, branch on `status` (§9). |
| Output | JSONL default; `bundle` profile; byte-faithful `content` | §8; fidelity contract §8.4 is absolute. |

**Environment note:** the Rust toolchain (cargo/rustc 1.95, Homebrew) and
libclang are already installed on the dev machine, but the sandbox's non-login
shell needs `export PATH="/opt/homebrew/bin:$PATH"` prepended to build commands.

---

## Crate layout

```
src/
  main.rs              cpp-navigator binary → cli::run()
  bin/cppnav.rs        cppnav alias        → cli::run()
  lib.rs               module wiring
  cli.rs               clap parser, global flags, exit-code mapping (§12, §9)
  commands/mod.rs      per-command pipelines + degradation ladder (§7, §9)
  search/mod.rs        Stage 0 candidate finder on ignore + grep (§5, §10)
  engine/
    mod.rs             Engine trait (the extensibility seam, §5)
    syntactic.rs       Stage 1 tree-sitter backend (§4, §11)
    semantic.rs        Stage 2 libclang backend  [feature = "semantic"]
  model.rs             internal types: Span, SourceRef, Symbol, Resolution (§6)
  output/mod.rs        wire format: Record envelope + JSONL/bundle Writer (§8)
```

Key dependencies: `clap`, `serde`/`serde_json`, `anyhow`, `thiserror`,
`ignore`, `grep`, `regex`, `rayon`, `tree-sitter`, `tree-sitter-cpp`; optional
`clang`; dev `tempfile`.

