## Phase 0 — Scaffold ✅

**Done.** Two binaries sharing `cli::run()`; clap CLI for all three commands and
every §12 global flag; internal data model (§6); wire format with JSONL/bundle
writer (§8); the `Engine` trait seam (§5); pipeline stubbed to `not_found`.
Exit codes verified (0 / 2 / 3).

---

## Phase 1 — Embedded ripgrep candidate finder ✅

**Done.** Stage 0 on ripgrep's own crates — no external `rg`.
- `ignore::WalkBuilder` parallel, gitignore-aware walk; `require_git(false)` so
  `.gitignore` applies even outside a git work tree.
- `grep` `RegexMatcher`/`Searcher` whole-word identifier line search.
- `bare_component()` peels `A::B::f → f` to maximize prefilter recall.
- `--max-candidates` distinct-file cap sets `truncated` and stops the walk.
- Deterministic ordering (file path, then byte offset).
- Wired into dispatch: text hits → fallback window, zero hits → `not_found`.

Verified on duckdb (4,943 files): sub-second; `.gitignore` honored; `--no-ignore`
reaches build artifacts; worst-case common identifier capped without hanging.

---

## Phase 2 — tree-sitter syntactic engine ✅

**Done.** Stage 1 default backend (`engine/syntactic.rs`).
- `SyntacticEngine` implements `Engine` (`definitions`/`declarations`/
  `enclosing_scope`); candidates parsed in parallel via rayon.
- Declarator-name matching peels pointer/reference/array wrappers, handles
  qualified `A::B::f`, operators, destructors (§11).
- Definition vs declaration by body/initializer presence.
- `template_declaration` span captured whole (prefix through body).
- find-decl extracts `signature`, `type` (`ret(params)`), adjacent Doxygen/comment.
- Resolver ladder in dispatch: 1 → `resolved`, >1 → `ambiguous`, 0-but-text →
  `fallback`, 0 → `not_found`.

Verified on duckdb: `NextPowerOfTwo`/`GetTypeIdSize` resolve with byte-fidelity
PASS; ubiquitous names correctly `ambiguous`; `find-decl MetaTransaction` resolves
with signature. 19 tests; clippy clean.

---

## Phase 3 — `--scope` class/struct expansion (find-def) ✅

**Done.** `enclosing_class_scope` added to the `Engine` trait + `SyntacticEngine`
(walks parents to the nearest `class_specifier`/`struct_specifier`, expands to a
wrapping `template_declaration`). `--scope` is threaded from `Command::FindDef`
into `resolve_one`; a resolved find-def member is widened via
`expand_to_class_scope`, re-slicing `content` from disk so §8.4 holds for the
wider span, and tagged with a scope message. Graceful no-op for free functions
and out-of-line members. Verified on duckdb: `find-def TupleData --scope` expands
the inline member to the whole `struct UpdateInfo` (byte-fidelity PASS);
`NextPowerOfTwo --scope` is unchanged. 24 tests; clippy clean.

**Goal:** implement PRD §2.3 / design §7.1 step 3 — when `--scope` is set and a
resolved definition is a class/struct member (or out-of-line member function),
expand the reported span to the **entire enclosing `class_specifier` /
`struct_specifier` / template** that houses the member.

**Work:**
- Add `enclosing_class_scope(file, byte_offset) -> Option<Span>` to
  `SyntacticEngine` (walk parents to nearest `class_specifier`/`struct_specifier`,
  expanding to a wrapping `template_declaration` if present). Distinct from the
  existing `enclosing_scope` (function/template) used by find-refs context.
- In `commands::resolve_one`, when `cli` carries `--scope` for `find-def`:
  after a `resolved` match, recompute the span via the class-scope lookup and
  rebuild the `content` bytes from the wider span. If the match is not inside a
  class/struct, return the member result unchanged (graceful no-op).
- Thread the `scope` flag from `Command::FindDef { scope }` into `resolve_one`
  (currently destructured away).
- Decide ambiguity interaction: `--scope` applies per resolved match; in the
  `ambiguous` case leave candidates as-is (member-level locations) for v1.

**Tests (unit):**
- Member function defined inline in a class → with `--scope`, span covers the
  whole `class { ... }`; without `--scope`, just the method.
- Out-of-line member (`void C::m() {}`) with `--scope` → still returns the method
  (its lexical encloser is the TU, not the class) — documents the known limit;
  semantic mode (Phase 7) is where cross-file class pull would live.
- Templated class member → span includes the `template<...>` prefix.
- Free function with `--scope` → unchanged (no enclosing class).
- Byte-fidelity assertion on the expanded span.

**Acceptance:**
- `find-def <member> --scope` on duckdb returns a class/struct body span whose
  `file[start_byte..end_byte]` round-trips byte-for-byte.
- Full `cargo test` + `cargo clippy` clean.

**Commit:** "Phase 3: --scope class/struct expansion for find-def".

---

## Phase 4 — find-decl polish ✅

**Done.** find-decl is now header-biased and emits richer declaration metadata.
- **Header bias:** `FinderConfig.prefer_headers` drives a header-only first pass
  (`.h/.hpp/.hh/.hxx`); only an empty header result falls back to a full search.
  Set for `Query::Declaration` in dispatch.
- **Qualified names from scope:** `enclosing_qualifier` walks `namespace`/`class`/
  `struct` ancestors so a namespace-qualified target (`duckdb::UpdateInfo`,
  `UpdateInfo::GetCompactCapacity`) matches a bare nested declaration; the result's
  `qualified_name` is populated.
- **Method vs member:** `field_declaration` prototypes classify as `Kind::Method`,
  data members as `Kind::Member`.
- **Type spelling:** `rendered_type` adds leading `const`/qualifiers and `*`/`&`/`&&`
  markers; trailing return types (`auto f() -> T`) are honored. Doc extraction
  already captured `///`/`//!` runs and `/** … */` blocks (now covered by tests).

Verified on duckdb: `find-decl UpdateInfo::GetCompactCapacity` resolves to the
header prototype (`update_info.hpp:101`, `type idx_t(idx_t)`); the bare name is
correctly `ambiguous` across two classes. 36 tests; clippy clean.

**Goal:** sharpen design §7.2 / §11 header handling and declaration metadata.

**Work:**
- **Header bias:** candidate finder ranks/searches header extensions
  (`.h/.hpp/.hh/.hxx`) first; fall back to all files if no header hit (§7.2 step 1).
  Implement as a two-pass finder or a post-sort preferring headers.
- **Doc extraction:** broaden beyond the immediate run — handle both `///`/`//!`
  line-doc runs and `/** ... */` block Doxygen; keep byte-faithful text.
- **Type spelling:** improve `ret(params)` for ref/ptr returns, `const`,
  trailing-return-type, and member-qualified signatures where syntactically clear.
- **Method vs free declaration:** populate `Kind::Method` for `field_declaration`
  prototypes; set `qualified_name` from enclosing namespace/class where available.

**Tests:** header-preferred resolution; block-comment doc; const/ref signatures;
member declaration kind + qualified name.

**Acceptance:** `find-decl` on duckdb headers returns signature + doc + type with
header paths preferred. Tests + clippy clean.

**Commit:** "Phase 4: find-decl header bias and richer declaration metadata".

---

## Phase 5 — find-refs (location-only + `--context`)

**Goal:** implement design §7.3 fully.

**Work:**
- **Location-only (default):** emit a dense per-hit record (or one record with a
  `locations: [{file, line}]` array — choose the more token-efficient shape and
  document it in the schema). No body parsing; this is the cheapest path (§7.3.2).
- **`--context`:** for each hit, use `enclosing_scope` (function/template) to emit
  the surrounding body span + byte-faithful `content` (§7.3.3).
- De-duplicate hits; keep deterministic ordering; respect `--max-candidates`
  with `truncated`.
- Filter out the definition site vs uses? v1: include all textual references
  (no semantic filtering); note the limitation.

**Tests:** location-only density; `--context` returns enclosing function span;
references across multiple files merged deterministically; fidelity on context.

**Acceptance:** `find-refs size --root duckdb` returns compact locations fast;
`--context` returns caller bodies. Tests + clippy clean.

**Commit:** "Phase 5: find-refs location-only and --context modes".

---

## Phase 6 — Output ergonomics

**Goal:** the human-in-the-loop transport features (design §3.2, §8.8–§8.10).

**Work:**
- **Bundle polish:** real token estimate footer (replace the `chars/4` heuristic
  with a defensible estimator); `--legend` one-time field key (§8.8).
- **Manifest / batch:** `--manifest <path>` (one query per line) and repeated
  targets; concatenate + de-duplicate; per-query headers in bundle mode (§8.9).
  One run → one paste.
- **Budget:** `--budget <n>` selection-only trim — prefer location-only over
  contextual, cap candidates, drop lowest-confidence; emit `budget_trimmed: true`
  + message; **never** edit payload bytes (§8.10, §8.4).

**Tests:** bundle round-trip; manifest parses + dedups; budget trims by selection
and sets the marker without altering any retained `content`.

**Acceptance:** a single `--manifest ... --format bundle --budget N` run produces
one paste-able block under the token cap. Tests + clippy clean.

**Commit:** "Phase 6: bundle/manifest/budget output ergonomics".

---

## Phase 7 — Stage 2 libclang + hardening ✅

**Goal:** the opt-in precision backend and the guarantees that survive review.

**Work:**
- **`engine/semantic.rs`** behind `#[cfg(feature = "semantic")]`: parse with
  libclang using `compile_commands.json`; resolve overloads/templates/namespaces
  to a single `resolved` where the build graph disambiguates (§4 Stage 2, §8.5
  note). Falls back to Stage 1 when DB/flags absent.
- Wire `--semantic` + `--compile-db`; select engine in dispatch; the default
  build (no feature) ignores the flag with a clear stderr note.
- **JSON Schema** for `schema_version` 1.0; validate emitted records in tests (§14).
- **Golden + fidelity tests** over fixture repos (§14).
- **Zero-egress CI guard:** run under a network-disabled sandbox / syscall
  monitor; fail on any `socket`/`connect` to non-local (§3.1, §14).
- **Perf benchmark** asserting sub-second point queries on a large synthetic tree.

**Acceptance:** `--features semantic --semantic` collapses a known overload to one
`resolved` on a fixture with a compile DB; schema validation + zero-egress test
green in CI; default build unchanged and self-contained.

**Commit(s):** "Phase 7: libclang semantic backend", "Phase 7: schema + zero-egress
CI + benchmarks" (may split).

---

## Cross-cutting conventions

- **Fidelity first:** any new `content`/`content_buffer` must satisfy
  `file[start_byte..end_byte) == bytes` (§8.4); add a fidelity assertion with each
  new span-producing path.
- **Graceful degradation:** never hard-fail when a lower rung can answer (§9).
- **Determinism:** sort merged results by `(file_path, start_byte)` for stable
  output across threads.
- **Per phase:** `cargo test` + `cargo clippy --all-targets` clean; a duckdb smoke
  test for the touched command; one focused commit; no push unless asked.
